=== SURFACE SUMMARY ===
  Native Apple-idiomatic SwiftUI parity of the Helix trip-planner card. The web source is an
  `AIFeatureCard` wrapped in `withAiFeature('trip-planner-llm-agent', …)` and driven by `useAiStream`;
  the native surface reproduces that composition, its data, its states, and its i18n. No networking
  lives in the view — it binds the `TripPlannerAgentModel` state holder (P1/S8).

  Data sources (web hooks → P1/S8 source seam; no direct HTTP from the view):
    • useTranslation → TripPlannerAgentStrings facade (P1/S10).
    • useAiStream    → TripPlannerAgentSource seam (start/stop/refresh + generate()=stream.start,
                       cancel()=stream.cancel; cancel fires on disappear, mirroring the web
                       AbortController-on-unmount). The view binds TripPlannerAgentModel only.

  Shared components used (web → native counterpart):
    • @/components/ai/AIFeatureCard  → header hoisted to the surface chrome with the freshness
      envelope; the action button + AiOutputPanel reproduced 1:1 (TripPlannerAgentActionButton /
      TripPlannerAgentOutputPanel / TripPlannerAgentThinkingView / TripPlannerAgentHelixBadge).
    • @/components/ai/withAiFeature  → the AI-enabled gate: TripPlannerAgentModel.isGated; when off the
      surface renders nothing (faithful web `return null`), unit-pinned.

  Charts / maps: none in the web source (the corridor map is a SIBLING surface, TripPlannerMap, out of
  scope here). This card is description + Ask-Helix button + streamed output only.

  Verbatim web logic ported + unit-pinned (the `useMemo` body + guards):
    request body (7 top-level fields, snake_case, POST /ai/trips/plan/draft):
      vehicle_id = numericVehicleId || 0 ; origin/destination = present ? {lat,lng,name:name??''}
      : {lat:0,lng:0,name:''} ; current_soc?80 ; charge_limit_soc?90 ; min_arrival_soc?20 ;
      speed_factor?1.0. canStart = haveInputs = !!vehicleId && origin != null && destination != null
      (a non-zero vehicle id AND both endpoints; negatives stay truthy, mirroring JS `!!(-3)`).
    Float fidelity: the body is encoded with JSONEncoder (shortest round-trippable form) so
      speed_factor 1.0 → "1" and a coordinate → "37.7749" — byte-faithful to JS JSON.stringify.
      (JSONSerialization would corrupt fractional doubles to "37.774900000000002" — proven + guarded
      by TripPlannerAgentRequestTests.testEncodedBodyPreservesFractionalCoordinatesLikeJSON.)
    SSE + reducer: port of parseSSEFrame / toTypedEvent + handleEvent / finalizeError — idle →
      streaming → (done | error); delta accumulates; confirm_request pauses; non-OK HTTP →
      "stream_http_{status}"; comments / malformed / unknown / tool_* dropped/no-op.

=== STATES (every non-gated one renders — no hidden surface) ===
  gated   — feature off → EmptyView (web withAiFeature → null), unit-pinned; not a hidden section.
  loading — useAiEnabled availability resolving → skeleton chrome (TripPlannerAgentLoadingView).
  error   — availability query failed → retryable gate error; terminal STREAM error renders inline as
            "Helix error: {message}" in the output panel.
  ready   — description + Ask-Helix button + output panel (empty / thinking / prose / error) + the
            orthogonal live/stale/offline connectivity axis (header freshness chip + banner with a
            one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
  empty   — gate open, no plan drafted → friendly hint ("No plan drafted yet…" with inputs, or
            "Select a vehicle, an origin, and a destination…" without) — never a blank box (P4).
  stale / offline — freshness chip + banner; stale auto-refreshes once, offline never.

